<%# locals: (faqs:) -%>
<div class="tldr"><p><strong>Snow Way's short answer:</strong> the best gifts for skiers are the things they use every run and don't think to buy for themselves: <strong>heated socks</strong>, <strong>rechargeable hand warmers</strong>, <strong>merino ski socks</strong>, a <strong>balaclava</strong>, <strong>goggles with a second lens</strong>, and a <strong>ski boot bag</strong>. Skip skis, boots and helmets as surprises, since they have to fit. For a skier who has everything, give lift days or a lesson.</p></div>
<p class="text-sm text-slate-400">Picks come from our gear guides, which summarize reviewers like Outdoor Life, Field &amp; Stream and GearJunkie. We don't test gear ourselves.</p>

<h2 id="stocking-stuffers">Stocking stuffers for skiers</h2>
<p>Small, cheap, and used every single ski day. These are the safest gifts because size barely matters.</p>
<table>
  <caption>Stocking stuffers for skiers</caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Gift</th><th scope="col">Why skiers like it</th><th scope="col">Our guide</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><th scope="row"><%= gear_link "HotHands hand warmers", "hothands hand warmers" %></th><td>Disposable packs for lift rides and cold toes. A box lasts a whole season.</td><td><%= link_to "Hand warmers", guide_path("best-hand-warmers") %></td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row"><%= gear_link "Merino ski socks", "merino ski socks" %></th><td>Thin, warm, and they don't smell after three days in boots. Skiers wear through them.</td><td><%= link_to "Ski socks", guide_path("best-ski-socks") %></td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row"><%= gear_link "Ski balaclava", "balaclava" %></th><td>Covers face, ears and neck under a helmet on windy, cold days.</td><td><%= link_to "Balaclava vs ski mask", guide_path("balaclava-vs-ski-mask") %></td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row"><%= gear_link "Neck gaiter", "neck gaiter" %></th><td>The lighter, more versatile option for milder days.</td><td><%= link_to "Balaclava vs ski mask", guide_path("balaclava-vs-ski-mask") %></td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row"><%= gear_link "Ski wax", "ski wax" %></th><td>For anyone who tunes their own skis. Pick a temperature range for where they ski, or an all-temperature wax.</td><td><%= link_to "How to wax skis", guide_path("how-to-wax-skis") %></td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2 id="everyday-gifts">Gifts they'll use every ski day</h2>
<table>
  <caption>Mid-range gifts for skiers</caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Gift</th><th scope="col">What to know</th><th scope="col">Our guide</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr><th scope="row"><%= gear_link "Fieldsheer Premium 2.0 Merino heated socks", "fieldsheer premium merino heated socks" %></th><td>Field &amp; Stream's best unisex heated sock, with app control. Listed around $80 by reviewers.</td><td><%= link_to "Heated socks", guide_path("best-heated-socks") %></td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row"><%= gear_link "OCOOPA UT3 PRO rechargeable hand warmer", "ocoopa ut3 pro hand warmer" %></th><td>A rechargeable warmer that replaces boxes of disposables. Check TSA rules if they fly.</td><td><%= link_to "Hand warmers", guide_path("best-hand-warmers") %></td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row"><%= gear_link "Goggles with interchangeable lenses", "ski goggles interchangeable lens" %></th><td>One lens for sun, one for flat light. If they wear glasses, get OTG goggles.</td><td><%= link_to "Ski goggles", guide_path("best-ski-goggles") %></td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row"><%= gear_link "Ski boot bag", "ski boot bags" %></th><td>Keeps boots, helmet and gloves together. A backpack style is easiest in airports.</td><td><%= link_to "Ski boot bags", guide_path("ski-boot-bag") %></td></tr>
    <tr><th scope="row"><%= gear_link "Heated ski gloves", "heated ski gloves" %></th><td>For skiers whose hands get cold first. Mittens run warmer than gloves.</td><td><%= link_to "Heated gloves", guide_path("best-heated-gloves") %></td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<h2 id="big-gifts">Bigger gifts</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong><%= gear_link "Hotronic XLP 2P heated socks", "hotronic xlp heated socks" %>:</strong> Outdoor Life's top heated ski sock, with a slim fit for ski boots and about 9 hours on high. Reviewers list it around $444.</li>
  <li><strong><%= gear_link "Heated boot bag", "heated boot bags" %>:</strong> warms boots before they go on, which makes cold parking-lot mornings a lot easier.</li>
  <li><strong><%= gear_link "Heated jacket or vest", "heated vest" %>:</strong> a heated vest under a shell is the more flexible pick. See our <%= link_to "heated jacket guide", guide_path("best-heated-jacket") %>.</li>
  <li><strong><%= gear_link "Ski tuning kit", "ski tuning kit" %>:</strong> for the skier who likes to tinker. Pair it with our <%= link_to "waxing how-to", guide_path("how-to-wax-skis") %>.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="not-gear">Gifts that aren't gear</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Lift days.</strong> Vail Resorts sells the Epic Day Pass for 1 to 7 days, from $50 to $106 a day, and December 6, 2026 is the last day to buy one this season. See <%= link_to "Ikon vs Epic", ikon_vs_epic_path %> for which pass fits where they ski.</li>
  <li><strong>A lesson.</strong> Even good skiers improve fast with one private lesson. Most resorts sell lessons online.</li>
  <li><strong>A trip.</strong> Pick a weekend at a resort they love. Our <%= link_to "best places to ski in December", "/best-places-to-ski-in-december" %> and <%= link_to "holiday ski trip guide", guide_path("holiday-ski-trips") %> help with timing.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="dont-buy">What not to buy as a surprise</h2>
<p>Skis, ski boots, helmets and ski jackets depend on height, weight, foot shape, ability and fit. A wrong guess is a hassle to return. If you want to give one of these, wrap a note or a gift card and shop together. Our <%= link_to "ski size chart", ski_size_chart_path %> helps if you're buying skis together.</p>

<% faqs << { question: "What are good gifts for skiers?", answer: "Things they use every ski day and rarely buy themselves: heated socks, rechargeable hand warmers, merino ski socks, a balaclava, goggles with a second lens, and a ski boot bag. Skip skis, boots and helmets as surprises because they have to fit." } %>
<% faqs << { question: "What are good stocking stuffers for skiers?", answer: "Disposable hand warmers like HotHands, merino ski socks, a balaclava or neck gaiter, and ski wax for anyone who tunes their own skis." } %>
<% faqs << { question: "What do you get a skier who has everything?", answer: "Heated socks, a heated boot bag, lift days or a lesson. Vail Resorts' Epic Day Pass runs from $50 to $106 a day for 1 to 7 days and is sold until December 6, 2026." } %>
<% faqs << { question: "Should I buy skis or ski boots as a gift?", answer: "Not as a surprise. Skis depend on height, weight and ability, and boots have to fit the person's feet. Give a note or a gift card and shop together." } %>
